# The library index and everything derived from it. This is the user's data,
# never source: index.db alone reaches half a gigabyte on a real library.
# It lives beside the app (<library>/_index/index.db), not inside it, but these
# patterns keep a stray copy out of a commit either way.
index.db
index.db-*
*.db
*.db.bak-*
# SQLite's side files. These are NOT matched by `*.db` (they end in -wal/-shm),
# and a copy of the index under any other name would otherwise be committed:
# a -wal without its database is a corrupt, meaningless blob.
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.db-journal

# Page embeddings, rebuilt with `py -3 studio.py embed`. The concept layer
# (concepts.npz / concepts.json) lives in the same per-library folder now; they
# stay listed here as well so a copy left in the app folder by an older install
# is still ignored.
vectors/
concepts.npz
concepts.json

# Machine-specific paths written by `studio.py paths --root ...`.
config.json

# Runtime output.
logs/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# Scratch output from the year-repair tooling.
yearfix_changes.csv